          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Dependent type theory is traditionally said to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            is not assumed in the theory, because once excluded middle holds, then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            are simply
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+booleans"} type of booleans
            resulting in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+mathematics"} impredicative
            foundations of mathematics. Function types into the type of booleans are in most versions of dependent type theory.
          %p
            The real problem here is with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+type"} dependent product type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            as the types from which they are formed from; i.e. if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U_i
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:U_i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B:U_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U_i
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:U_i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B:U_{i+1}
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+predicative+mathematics"} strongly predicative
                dependent type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+predicative+mathematics"} strongly predicative mathematics
          %p
            In strongly predicative dependent type theory, the resulting universes of
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+pretopos"} arithmetic pretopos
            instead of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CE%A0W-pretopos"} ΠW-pretopos
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Vickers"} Steve Vickers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+mathematics"} geometric mathematics
            occurs informally inside of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            and does not assume function types for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topological
            reasons, and he has proposed a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+type+theory"} geometric type theory
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of said Grothendieck topos (
            %a{:href => "#Vickers07"}> Vickers 2007
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Vickers17"} Vickers 2017
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Vickers18"} Vickers 2018
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Vickers22"} Vickers 2022
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrik+Buchholtz"} Ulrik Buchholtz
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johannes+Schipp+von+Branitz"} Johannes Schipp von Branitz
            have proposed a version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            where the base universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_0
            does not contain any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/primitive+recursive+arithmetic"} primitive recursive arithmetic
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#BvB24"}> Buchholtz &amp; von Branitz 2024
            ).
          %h2#formal_presentation Formal presentation
          %p
            We present strongly predicative dependent type theory as a dependent type theory with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+of+universes"} hierarchy of universes
            and no
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Book+HoTT"} Book HoTT
            found in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#UFP13"} Univalent Foundations Project 2013
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theoretic+axiom+of+replacement"} type theoretic axiom of replacement
            from
            %a{:href => "#BBCDG"} Bezem et al 2021
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rijke22"} Rijke 2022
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+sets"} quotient sets
            in all universes.
          %p
            The type theory has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgments"} judgments
            for contexts
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}
              , that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
          %h3#universe_levels_and_peano_arithmetic  Universe levels and Peano arithmetic
          %p Then we have judgments for universe levels and predicate logic:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \; \mathrm{level}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                is a universe level,
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \; \mathrm{prop}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \; \mathrm{true}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
                proposition,
          %p
            and the formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} signature
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+arithmetic"} Heyting arithmetic
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peano+arithmetic"} Peano arithmetic
          %p
            These rules ensure that there are an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite"} infinite
            number of indices, which are strictly ordered with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+total+order"} strict total order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            and upwardly unbounded, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \lt s(i)
            is true for all indices
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %h3#typing_judgments_and_russell_universes Typing judgments and Russell universes
          %p
            Now, we introduce the typing judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is a term of the type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universe"} Russell universe
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level}}{\Gamma \vdash U_i:U_{s(i)}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i}{\Gamma \vdash A:U_{s(i)}}
          %p In addition, we have rules for contexts which state that one could add typing judgments to the list of contexts:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i}{(\Gamma, a:A) \; \mathrm{ctx}}
          %h3#structural_rules Structural rules
          %p
            There are three structural rules in dependent type theory, the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable+rule"} variable rule
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakening+rule"} weakening rule
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution+rule"} substitution rule
          %p The variable rule states that we may derive a typing judgment if the typing judgment is in the context already:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \vdash a:A}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{J}
            be any arbitrary judgment. Then we have the following rules:
          %p The weakening rule:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}
          %p The substitution rule:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash a:A \quad \Gamma, b:A, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}{\Gamma, \Delta[a/b] \vdash \mathcal{J}[a/b]}
          %p The weakening and substitution rules are admissible rules: they do not need to be explicitly included in the type theory as they could be proven by induction on the structure of all possible derivations.
          %h3#structural_rules_for_judgmental_equality Structural rules for judgmental equality
          %p Judgmental equality has its own structural rules: introduction rules for judgmentally equal terms, reflexivity, symmetry, transitivity, the principle of substitution, and the variable conversion rule.
          %ul
            %li
              %p Introduction rules for judgmentally equal terms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma \vdash a \equiv b:A}{\Gamma \vdash a:A}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma \vdash a \equiv b:A}{\Gamma \vdash b:A}
            %li
              %p Reflexivity of judgmental equality
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma \vdash a:A}{\Gamma \vdash a \equiv a:A}
            %li
              %p Symmetry of judgmental equality
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi b
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma \vdash a \equiv b:A}{\Gamma \vdash b \equiv a:A}
            %li
              %p Transitivity of judgmental equality
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi b
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi c
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi c
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma \vdash a \equiv b:A \quad \Gamma \vdash b \equiv c:A}{\Gamma \vdash a \equiv c:A}
            %li
              %p Principle of substitution:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi c
                          %mo :
                          %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo :
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A:U_i \quad \Gamma \vdash a \equiv b : A \quad \Gamma, x:A, \Delta \vdash c:B}{\Gamma, \Delta[b/x] \vdash c[a/x] \equiv c[b/x]: B[b/x]}
            %li
              %p Variable conversion rule:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo ≡
                          %mi B
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi 𝒥
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi B
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi 𝒥
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash A \equiv B:U_i \quad \Gamma, x:A, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}{\Gamma, x:B, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}
          %p We also have a rules saying that equality is preserved across universe levels:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ≡
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash i \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash j \; \mathrm{level} \quad \Gamma \vdash i = j \; \mathrm{true}}{\Gamma \vdash U_i \equiv U_j:U_{s(i)}}
          %h3#dependent_product_types Dependent product types
          %p
            The key difference in strongly predicative dependent type theory from the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+predicative+mathematics"} weakly predicative
            dependent type theory comes in the formation rule of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U_i
            and type family
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash B(x):U_i
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{s(i)}
          %ul
            %li Formation rules for dependent product types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
